The golden rule: Initialize weights to small random values but never to zero.
If you initialize all weights in a layer to zero (or any identical number), every neuron in that layer will compute the exact same output


Just picking random numbers isn't enough; the scale (variance) of those random numbers must match the activation function you are using.

